NEW[62] = ("Rarefaction was repeated rather than drawn once [44], and metrics rather than count tables were averaged, since averaging tables would inflate observed richness above what 3,000 reads can support: alpha indices over 1,000 rarefactions, Bray–Curtis and Jaccard matrices over 400, and unweighted UniFrac, weighted normalized UniFrac and Faith's phylogenetic diversity over 400 draws run as two independent chains. Monte-Carlo error, measured between independent chains, was negligible relative to the technical and biological dissimilarities (Supplementary Table S5; details in Supplementary Note S2).")
